  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 3: Reasoning with an LLM\n",
    "\n",
    "## Goal\n",
    "Feed the transcribed question into a small language model (LLM) to generate an intelligent response.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Model Choice\n",
    "We'll use **TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat** because it:\n",
    "- Runs efficiently in Colab (only 1.1B parameters)\n",
    "- Is fine-tuned for chat/instruction following\n",
    "- Produces coherent, contextual answers\n",
    "\n",
    "Alternative options:\n",
    "- `distilgpt2` (smaller, faster, less coherent)\n",
    "- `facebook/opt-1.3b` (similar size)\n",
    "- `google/flan-t5-base` (encoder-decoder, good for Q&A)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load TinyLlama model and tokenizer\n",
    "print(\"📥 Loading TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat model...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "model_name = \"TinyLlama/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0\"\n",
    "\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name)\n",
    "llm_model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n",
    "    model_name,\n",
    "    torch_dtype=torch.float16 if device == \"cuda\" else torch.float32,\n",
    "    device_map=\"auto\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✅ TinyLlama loaded on {device}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Parameters: 1.1B\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Context window: 2048 tokens\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Architecture: Llama-2 based\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create a prompt template for the LLM\n",
    "def create_chat_prompt(question):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Format the user's question using TinyLlama's chat template.\n",
    "    TinyLlama uses the ChatML format:\n",
    "    <|system|>\\n{system_message}</s>\\n<|user|>\\n{user_message}</s>\\n<|assistant|>\\n\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    system_message = (\n",
    "        \"You are a helpful AI assistant. Provide clear, concise, and informative answers. \"\n",
    "        \"Keep responses under 100 words and be specific.\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    \n",
    "    prompt = f\"\"\"<|system|>\n",
    "{system_message}</s>\n",
    "<|user|>\n",
    "{question}</s>\n",
    "<|assistant|>\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "    return prompt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test the prompt\n",
    "prompt = create_chat_prompt(user_question)\n",
    "print(\"📝 Formatted Prompt:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
    "print(prompt)\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 60)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generate LLM response\n",
    "print(\"🤖 Generating LLM response...\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Tokenize input\n",
    "inputs = tokenizer(prompt, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate response\n",
    "with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "    outputs = llm_model.generate(\n",
    "        **inputs,\n",
    "        max_new_tokens=150,  # Limit response length\n",
    "        temperature=0.7,     # Control randomness (0.7 = balanced)\n",
    "        top_p=0.9,          # Nucleus sampling\n",
    "        do_sample=True,     # Enable sampling for varied responses\n",
    "        pad_token_id=tokenizer.eos_token_id,\n",
    "        repetition_penalty=1.2  # Reduce repetitive text\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "# Decode the response\n",
    "full_response = tokenizer.decode(outputs[0], skip_special_tokens=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Extract only the assistant's response (after <|assistant|>)\n",
    "if \"<|assistant|>\" in full_response:\n",
    "    llm_answer = full_response.split(\"<|assistant|>\")[-1].strip()\n",
    "    # Remove any trailing special tokens\n",
    "    llm_answer = llm_answer.replace(\"</s>\", \"\").strip()\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    llm_answer = full_response\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(\"🤖 LLM RESPONSE:\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "print(f\"{llm_answer}\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*60)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Store for TTS\n",
    "tts_input_text = llm_answer"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Reflection: Task 3\n",
    "\n",
    "**What worked:**\n",
    "- TinyLlama generates contextually relevant responses\n",
    "- Chat template ensures proper instruction following\n",
    "- Model runs efficiently even in free Colab tier\n",
    "\n",
    "**Performance:**\n",
    "- Inference latency: ~2-5 seconds on GPU for 100 tokens\n",
    "- Temperature 0.7 balances creativity and coherence\n",
    "- Top-p sampling (0.9) focuses on most likely tokens\n",
    "\n",
    "**Quality observations:**\n",
    "- Responses are generally coherent for a 1.1B model\n",
    "- May occasionally produce generic or incomplete answers\n",
    "- For better quality, consider:\n",
    "  - Larger models (Llama-2-7B, Mistral-7B) if GPU memory permits\n",
    "  - Few-shot prompting with examples\n",
    "  - Fine-tuning on domain-specific Q&A data\n",
    "\n",
    "**Potential issues:**\n",
    "- Repetition (mitigated with repetition_penalty=1.2)\n",
    "- Off-topic responses (improved with clear system prompt)\n",
    "- Memory limits on large context (2048 token limit)\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 4: Text-to-Speech (TTS)\n",
    "\n",
    "## Goal\n",
    "Convert the LLM's text response into spoken audio using **SpeechT5**.\n",
    "\n",
    "## TTS Pipeline Components\n",
    "1. **SpeechT5Processor**: Tokenizes text\n",
    "2. **SpeechT5ForTextToSpeech**: Generates speech representations\n",
    "3. **SpeechT5HifiGan**: Vocoder that converts representations to audio waveform\n",
    "4. **Speaker Embedding**: Controls voice characteristics (pitch, timbre, accent)\n",
    "\n",
    "## Process Flow\n",
    "```\n",
    "Text → Tokens → Speech Features → Waveform (16 kHz)\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load SpeechT5 models\n",
    "print(\"📥 Loading SpeechT5 TTS models...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "processor = SpeechT5Processor.from_pretrained(\"microsoft/speecht5_tts\")\n",
    "tts_model = SpeechT5ForTextToSpeech.from_pretrained(\"microsoft/speecht5_tts\").to(device)\n",
    "vocoder = SpeechT5HifiGan.from_pretrained(\"microsoft/speecht5_hifigan\").to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ SpeechT5 models loaded successfully\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Device: {device}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Output sample rate: 16,000 Hz\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load speaker embeddings (voice characteristics)\n",
    "print(\"🎭 Loading speaker embeddings...\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load pre-computed speaker embeddings from CMU ARCTIC dataset\n",
    "embeddings_dataset = load_dataset(\n",
    "    \"Matthijs/cmu-arctic-xvectors\",\n",
    "    split=\"validation\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Use a specific speaker (you can experiment with different indices 0-7185)\n",
    "speaker_embedding = torch.tensor(\n",
    "    embeddings_dataset[7306][\"xvector\"]\n",
    ").unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✅ Speaker embedding loaded\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Shape: {speaker_embedding.shape}\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Embedding dimension: 512\")\n",
    "print(f\"   Speaker ID: 7306 (clear female voice)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generate speech from text\n",
    "print(f\"🔊 Generating speech for: '{tts_input_text[:100]}...'\\n\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Tokenize input text\n",
